    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for pgadmin4",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for pgadmin4 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2025-12765: insufficient checks in the LDAP authentication flow allow a for bypass of TLS certificate validation\n  that can lead to the stealing of bind credentials and the altering of directory responses (bsc#1253478).\n- CVE-2025-12764: improper validation of characters in a username allows for LDAP injections that force the processing\n  of unusual amounts of data and leads to a DoS (bsc#1253477).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
